-- title:
--   Character intertwiners of restricted induced corners preserve mass
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be the constructed restricted-product measure, let $A,B$ be measurable corners of finite mass, and fix a compact sequence-solenoid parameter $k$. If an actual unitary between their induced $L^2$ spaces intertwines every character phase multiplier with parameter $k$ and every rational counting-index shift, then
--   $$M(A)=M(B).$$
--   This supplies the trace comparison using exactly the generators occurring in the explicit induced family.
